FFmpeg
------
The Docker image includes FFmpeg (the `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe` programs), installed from Debian bookworm's `ffmpeg`
package. Debian builds it with `--enable-gpl` and `--enable-libx264`, so those binaries are licensed under the GNU
General Public License.

Docket runs `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe` only as separate programs to read, clean and take posters from uploaded videos.
It does not link to them, and Docket's own code stays MIT licensed. This notice states what Docket does; it is not a
legal conclusion.

Corresponding source
--------------------
The corresponding source is Debian's `ffmpeg` source package for the shipped version (for example
`7:5.1.9-0+deb12u1`):

  https://sources.debian.org/src/ffmpeg/
  `apt-get source ffmpeg` on Debian bookworm

The exact version in an image is shown by `dpkg -s ffmpeg` inside it.
